    <!-- Date Changes -->
    <section class="content-section" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <h2>Why Dates Can Change During WIB to EST Conversion</h2>
      <p>
        Because WIB is 12 hours ahead of EST, morning hours in WIB correspond to the previous calendar day in EST.
      </p>
      <h3>Date Rollover Window</h3>
      <ul style="padding-left: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.9;">
        <li><strong>WIB 00:00 to 11:59 AM</strong> → EST 12:00 PM to 11:59 PM → <strong>Previous calendar day</strong></li>
        <li><strong>WIB 12:00 PM (Noon)</strong> → EST 00:00 (Midnight) → <strong>Same calendar day</strong></li>
        <li><strong>WIB 18:00 (6:00 PM)</strong> → EST 06:00 AM → <strong>Same calendar day</strong></li>
        <li><strong>WIB 23:00 (11:00 PM)</strong> → EST 11:00 AM → <strong>Same calendar day</strong></li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Always check both the <strong>time and date</strong> when communicating across WIB and EST. Our converter tool updates calendar dates automatically.
      </p>
    </section>

