      </p>
      <h3>Overlapping Working Hours</h3>
      <p>
        A 12-hour difference means standard working hours in Jakarta (8:00 AM to 5:00 PM WIB) correspond to <strong>8:00 PM to 5:00 AM EST</strong>. The best window for real-time communication occurs at <strong>6:00 PM to 8:00 PM WIB (6:00 AM to 8:00 AM EST)</strong>, when Indonesian teams wrap up their evening while U.S. East Coast teams start their morning.
      </p>
      <h3>Technical Systems Context</h3>
      <p>
        Cloud platforms and financial APIs operating in Southeast Asia convert transaction timestamps stored in WIB or UTC to EST for U.S. corporate reporting. Using a date-aware calculation ensures accurate audit logs.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Common Mistakes -->
