      <h2>Common WIB to EST Conversion Mistakes</h2>
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem;">
        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem;">❌ Adding Instead of Subtracting</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">EST is 12 hours behind WIB. You must subtract 12 hours from WIB. Adding 12 hours gives UTC+19, which is incorrect.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem;">❌ Missing Previous-Day Rollover</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">WIB times from 00:00 to 11:59 AM belong to the previous calendar day in EST. Always verify the date.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem;">❌ Confusing WIB with WITA or WIT</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">Indonesia has 3 time zones. WIB is UTC+7 (Jakarta), WITA is UTC+8 (Bali), and WIT is UTC+9 (Papua). Using WIB for Bali creates a 1-hour error.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem;">❌ Confusing EST with EDT</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">EST is UTC-5 (winter). EDT is UTC-4 (summer). Using EST during summer introduces a 1-hour shift relative to New York local clocks.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

